@frasercrone3838 I was kind of on the same thought process. How do we know how good the work is? how do we know it will hold up since nothing was torqued to spec. My major concerns was the crank and the head... if those bolts let loose on either that engine is toast.

Also, it looked like they reused the same head gasket and just doctored it up with some glue.

Maybe this thing will last another year or two and judging by the condition of the oil when they cracked it open it seems no one really gives AF about basic maintenance so if this el cheapo rebuild lasts 1 year they probably get their money out of it.

